      "hasMediaInOriginal": false,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "⚡️🇺🇸 FTC sues Amazon over $20 billion hidden advertising surcharge scheme\n\nThe U.S. Federal Trade Commission and 22 state attorneys general have sued Amazon, accusing the company of secretly manipulating its advertising auctions to overcharge more than 1.2 million advertisers since 2019.\n\nThe FTC alleges Amazon told advertisers they were using a “second-price” auction, where the winning advertiser would pay only slightly more than the next-highest bid. Instead, Amazon introduced a hidden “soft reserve price” that allowed it to raise the final price, potentially extracting more than $20 billion from advertisers.\n\nThe FTC says the higher advertising costs were ultimately passed on to consumers through higher product prices. More than 500,000 small and medium-sized businesses were among those affected.\n\n@medmannews",
